==== Build OpenVPN client image ====

It is possible to build a restricted image without Luci and IPv6 but including OpenVPN client. :!: It was tested on TL-WR741ND v4.2 only :!:

Prepare build environment, you need at least 9 Gb of free space to build the image. As build requires gcc/g++ version 4.8 the simple way of getting it is using ''ubuntu:18.04'' docker container:
<code>docker run --name openwrt -ti ubuntu:18.04</code>
Install necessary prerequisites [[docs:guide-developer:toolchain:install-buildsystem#debianubuntu]], install GCC 4.8:
<code>apt-get install gcc-4.8 g++-4.8</code>
Switch to the proper GCC versions:
<code>
export GCC=gcc-4.8
export GXX=g++-4.8
</code>
Clone OpenWrt code and checkout 18.06 tag:
<code>
git clone https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt.git
cd openwrt
git checkout openwrt-18.06
</code>
Download and unpack config :!: version 4 :!: {{ :media:tplink:tl-wr741:tl-wr741nd-v4-openvpn-config.tgz |}}, put it into openwrt git repo directory. This config is made from default one by removing all IPv6 and Luci packages and adding OpenVPN and OpenSSL.
Finally build the image:
<code>
./scripts/feeds update -a
./scripts/feeds install -a
make
</code>
Find the result in ''./bin/targets/ar71xx/tiny''.

